Template: ocm/pki_dir
Type: string
Default: /etc/openvpn/easy-rsa/pki
Description: Path to your existing easy-rsa PKI:
 OCM issues and revokes client certificates from the CA your OpenVPN server
 already uses. It never creates a CA of its own.
 .
 This directory must contain ca.crt and private/ca.key.

Template: ocm/openvpn_dir
Type: string
Default: /etc/openvpn
Description: OpenVPN configuration directory:
 Where your server configuration lives. OCM reads it to build client profiles
 that match the running server; the configuration itself is never modified.

Template: ocm/vpn_host
Type: string
Description: Public hostname or IP clients connect to:
 Used as the "remote" line of the generated .ovpn profiles. Use the public DNS
 name or static IP your VPN clients can reach.

Template: ocm/http_port
Type: string
Default: 80
Description: HTTP port for the OCM web console:

Template: ocm/bind_addr
Type: string
Default: 127.0.0.1
Description: Address the web console binds to:
 The console is served over plain HTTP. The default (127.0.0.1) exposes it
 locally only, reachable through an SSH tunnel:
 .
     ssh -L 8080:127.0.0.1:<port> root@<server>
 .
 Use 0.0.0.0 to listen on every interface - only do so behind a TLS reverse
 proxy or a firewall that restricts who can reach the port.
